</span>Introduction</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Understanding ai pet training</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><p>Most training advice is generic. It assumes an average animal, an average handler and an average environment, and then fails quietly when your dog is fearful, your schedule is irregular or your cues are inconsistent.</p><p>PawlogicTech builds a programme around measured learning rate, tracks reliability under real-world distraction, and adjusts difficulty automatically so sessions stay in the productive zone.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-background p-8 sm:p-10"><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted-foreground">The problem</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl leading-snug sm:text-3xl">Why training plateaus</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Progress stalls for predictable reasons: sessions are too long, criteria are raised too quickly, reinforcement is inconsistent, or the behaviour was never generalised beyond the kitchen.</p><ul class="mt-6 space-y-3"><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-muted-foreground"></span>Owners raise difficulty faster than the animal is ready for.</li><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-muted-foreground"></span>Reliability is judged in easy environments and assumed everywhere else.</li><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-muted-foreground"></span>Reinforcement timing drifts by seconds, which is an eternity to a dog.</li><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-muted-foreground"></span>There is no measurement, so nobody notices the plateau for weeks.</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-3xl bg-primary p-8 text-primary-foreground sm:p-10"><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Our solution</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl leading-snug sm:text-3xl">Measured, adaptive, reward-based programmes</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/75">Every repetition is logged. The system tracks success rate per cue per environment and only raises criteria when performance justifies it, using exclusively positive reinforcement methods.</p><ul class="mt-6 space-y-3"><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Difficulty adjusted automatically from measured success rate.</li><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Generalisation tracked separately for each environment.</li><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Session length capped at the point where attention measurably drops.</li><li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Reinforcement timing feedback for the handler, not just the animal.</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Benefits</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What you get out of it</h2></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift"><h3 class="text-xl">Faster acquisition</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Correctly paced criteria progression is the single biggest driver of learning speed.</p></div><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift"><h3 class="text-xl">Genuine reliability</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">A cue that works in the park, not only in the kitchen.</p></div><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift"><h3 class="text-xl">Humane by design</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Reward-based only. No aversive methods, ever.</p></div><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift"><h3 class="text-xl">Consistent households</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Everyone in the home follows the same cues and criteria.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-secondary"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Features</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Everything included as standard</h2></div><dl class="grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2"><div><dt class="font-display text-lg">Adaptive difficulty</dt><dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-sage-foreground/80">Criteria raised or lowered from live success-rate data.</dd></div><div><dt class="font-display text-lg">Cue re