ing-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Who needs this</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Households and organisations this is built for</h2></div><dl class="mt-8 space-y-6"><div class="rule-accent"><dt class="font-display text-xl">New puppies</dt><dd class="mt-1.5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Owners who want to get the critical first sixteen weeks right.</dd></div><div class="rule-accent"><dt class="font-display text-xl">Rescue dogs</dt><dd class="mt-1.5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Animals needing confidence building and foundation cues from an unknown starting point.</dd></div><div class="rule-accent"><dt class="font-display text-xl">Working handlers</dt><dd class="mt-1.5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">People with irregular schedules who need short, high-yield sessions.</dd></div><div class="rule-accent"><dt class="font-display text-xl">Cat owners</dt><dd class="mt-1.5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Carrier training, husbandry cooperation and enrichment for indoor cats.</dd></div></dl></div><img alt="Veterinary professional reviewing ai pet training data for a patient" class="w-full rounded-3xl object-cover shadow-lift" decoding="async" height="900" loading="lazy" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_template_directory_uri() ); ?>/assets/images/vet-review.webp" width="1200"/></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-3xl"><p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Why PawlogicTech</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Clinically governed, privacy-first, and deliberately quiet</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/75">Every threshold in AI Pet Training is reviewed by our veterinary advisory panel before release. We tune for clinical usefulness rather than notification volume, we compare your animal only against itself, and we never sell your data. Everything exports, because the record belongs to you and should follow your animal wherever it goes.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24" id="faq"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>FAQ</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">AI Pet Training questions, answered</h2></div><div class="divide-y divide-border rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card"><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">Does PawlogicTech use any aversive methods?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">No. The platform is exclusively reward-based. We do not support or integrate with shock, prong, spray or vibration correction devices, and we will not generate programmes that rely on aversive techniques.</p></details><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">How much time does it take each day?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Three to five sessions of two to five minutes each. Short and frequent consistently outperforms one long daily session, and the scheduler is built around that finding.</p></details><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">Can it train a cat?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Yes. Cats train well with reward-based shaping. The feline curriculum focuses on carrier acceptance, cooperative care, recall and enrichment.</p></details><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">What if progress stalls?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The system detects plateaus automatically and lowers criteria to rebuild success rate before progressing again, which is exactly the correction most owners miss.</p></details></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Related services</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Services that pair well with this one</h2></div><ul class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3"><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/services/ai-pet-health-monitoring/' ) ); ?>"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-xl">AI Pet Health Monitoring</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Continuous vitals, early-warning alerts and vet-ready health records.</p></div></a></li><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/services/ai-behavior-analysis/' ) ); ?>"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-xl">AI Behavior Analysis</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Understand anxiety, aggression and stress through measured behaviour.</p></div></a></li><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/services/smart-pet-care/' ) ); ?>"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-xl">Smart Pet Care</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Connected feeding, hydration, climate and daily-care automation.</p></div></a></li></ul></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Further reading</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Articles from our veterinary and behavioural team</h2></div><ul class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3"><li><article><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Pet Health · 8 min read</p><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl leading-snug"><a class="hover:text-accent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/blog/early-signs-of-illness-in-dogs/' ) ); ?>">The Early Signs of Illness in Dogs Most Owners Miss</a></h3><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">By the time a dog looks unwell, the condition has usually been developing for weeks. These are the eight signals that appear first, and why almost nobody notices them.</p></article></li><li><article><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Behaviour · 7 min read</p><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl leading-snug"><a class="hover:text-accent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/blog/how-ai-detects-pet-anxiety/' ) ); ?>">How AI Detects Pet Anxiety Before You Do</a></h3><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The behaviour you most need to understand happens when nobody is home. Measurement solves a problem that observation structurally cannot.</p></article></li><li><article><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Nutrition · 6 min read</p><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl leading-snug"><a class="hover:text-accent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/blog/smart-feeding-and-pet-obesity/' ) ); ?>">Smart Feeding and the Pet Obesity Problem</a></h3><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Nobody intends to overfeed. Portion drift is a measurement failure, not a discipline failure, and measurement is the thing that fixes it.</p></article></li></ul></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-primary px-8 py-16 text-primary-foreground sm:px-14"><span aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-24 -top-24 h-72 w-72 rounded-full bg-accent/25 blur-3xl"></span><div class="relative max-w-2xl"><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Ready to put AI Pet Training to work?</h2><p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/75">A short consultation tells us your animal, your household and your goal. We will recommend the smallest configuration that solves it.</p><div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-accent-foreground transition-transform duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="<?php echo esc_u